## Key Concepts

- **Offline-first sync architecture**: Prioritizes local-first writes with eventual consistency to remote
- **TurboModule/JSI bridges**: Enables synchronous, type-safe native communication without bridge serialization overhead
- **Local SQLite queue**: Tracks pending changes with timestamps and operation types for reliable sync
- **Conflict resolution strategies**: Version vectors for causality tracking; CRDT or last-write-wins for merge semantics
- **Schema migrations**: Additive migrations with backward compatibility; migration scripts stored in versioned history table
- **Background workers**: Dedicated threads prevent UI jank during heavy I/O operations
- **Backpressure handling**: Bounded queue sizes with configurable flush thresholds

